('Noise expectations for shared homes', paras('A silver bullet can be discreet in a drawer but still noticeable during use. Sound depends on motor quality, speed, surface contact, room acoustics, and whether the device rattles against hard objects. Product pages rarely give lab-grade noise measurements, so practical clues matter.', 'Look for reviews that mention roommates, thin walls, or late-night use. A soft storage pouch, lower settings, and avoiding hard surfaces can reduce vibration transfer. If quiet use is essential, compare with guides focused specifically on quiet vibrators.')),
('Charging, batteries, and travel storage', paras('Rechargeable bullets should list charger type, charge time, run time, and water-resistance limits. Magnetic chargers are convenient but easy to lose. Battery-powered bullets should explain battery size and safe replacement. Do not mix old and new batteries, and remove batteries before long storage when the manual recommends it.', 'For travel, power the device off, use a pouch, and keep chargers organized. TSA guidance for personal electronics is a useful reminder that lithium-ion devices and batteries should be packed responsibly. Avoid traveling with mystery chargers or damaged battery compartments.')),
('Cleaning and lubricant compatibility', paras('Cleaning instructions should be specific. Waterproof, water-resistant, and splashproof do not mean the same thing. If the product has a charging port, battery cap, or seam, follow the manual closely and dry it fully before storage.', 'Water-based lubricant is often a practical default because it is compatible with many toy materials and cleans up easily. Do not use harsh household cleaners. If a product page cannot explain cleaning or lubricant compatibility, choose a clearer listing.')),
